WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.334 --> 00:00:19.367
"You cowards!" cried Captain Hook. Grabbing a lantern, he raised his claw.

2
00:00:19.368 --> 00:00:25.991
"I'll bring that thing out here myself." Hook angrily dashed into the cabin.

3
00:00:25.992 --> 00:00:29.836
"Five?" wondered Slightly.

4
00:00:29.837 --> 00:00:34.890
But soon Hook came staggering out without his lantern.

5
00:00:34.891 --> 00:00:39.342
"Something blew out my light," he said nervously.

6
00:00:39.343 --> 00:00:42.904
"What about Cecco?" asked Noodler.

7
00:00:42.905 --> 00:00:48.103
"He's as dead as Bill Jukes," replied Hook.

8
00:00:48.104 --> 00:00:53.360
The pirates were scared, but they saw that Hook was afraid too.

9
00:00:53.361 --> 00:00:55.935
They started to make fun of him.

10
00:00:55.936 --> 00:01:01.267
The mutiny that Captain Hook had joked about seemed to be really happening.

11
00:01:01.268 --> 00:01:05.088
"Are you scared, Captain Hook?" asked Cookson.

12
00:01:05.089 --> 00:01:09.139
"They say that a ship is cursed when a stranger is aboard.

13
00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:12.738
Does the crowing thing have crocodile teeth and a tail?"

14
00:01:12.739 --> 00:01:18.361
"Does it have a hook?" asked Robert Mullins. "Is it the devil?"

15
00:01:18.362 --> 00:01:23.889
"This ship is doomed! Let's mutiny!" cried Skylights.

16
00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:31.542
One by one, all the pirates repeated the cry: "We're doomed! Mutiny!"

17
00:01:31.543 --> 00:01:35.312
Hearing the pirates, the boys let out a cheer.

18
00:01:35.313 --> 00:01:41.645
But Hook wasn't beaten yet, and his face lit up with a wicked idea.

19
00:01:41.646 --> 00:01:51.594
He looked at the boys. "My sweet lads," he said, in an evil tone, turning to his pirates.

20
00:01:51.595 --> 00:01:55.924
"Open the cabin door and push the prisoners in.

21
00:01:55.925 --> 00:02:01.122
Let them fight the crowing thing! If they kill it, wonderful!

22
00:02:01.123 --> 00:02:06.456
If it kills them, we are no worse than before."

23
00:02:06.457 --> 00:02:11.786
The brilliance of this plan surprised the other pirates, and they stopped their mutiny.

24
00:02:11.787 --> 00:02:15.034
For one last time, they obeyed.

25
00:02:15.035 --> 00:02:23.431
Still chained, the boys pretended to struggle but allowed themselves to be pushed into the cabin.

26
00:02:23.432 --> 00:02:27.987
With a yell, the pirates closed the cabin door.

27
00:02:27.988 --> 00:02:34.427
"Now let's listen!" cried Hook. He stepped back and they all turned away.

28
00:02:34.428 --> 00:02:39.486
Even though the door was closed, none of the pirates could bear to look at it.

29
00:02:39.487 --> 00:02:44.289
They listened, waiting for the screams and the crowing.

30
00:02:44.290 --> 00:02:49.019
Meanwhile Wendy, still bound to the mast, watched.

31
00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:54.529
She wasn't waiting for the screams or the crowing, but for Peter to appear.

32
00:02:54.530 --> 00:02:58.837
She knew he had come to save them all.

33
00:02:58.838 --> 00:03:05.813
Inside the cabin, Peter found what he had hoped would be there—the keys to free the boys.

34
00:03:05.814 --> 00:03:12.437
After Peter removed their chains, the boys found some weapons and snuck out onto the deck.

35
00:03:12.438 --> 00:03:15.681
Hook and the pirates still had their backs turned.

36
00:03:15.682 --> 00:03:21.447
The boys hid, while Peter crept to the mast and cut Wendy's ropes.

37
00:03:21.448 --> 00:03:26.632
Now Peter, the boys, and Wendy were free to fly back home.

38
00:03:26.633 --> 00:03:32.475
But Peter remembered his vow: "This time, it's Hook or me!"

39
00:03:32.476 --> 00:03:37.363
Wendy joined the boys in hiding, and Peter took her place at the mast.

40
00:03:37.364 --> 00:03:45.005
He put her cloak around him, covered his head, took a deep breath, and crowed loudly.

41
00:03:45.006 --> 00:03:53.503
Hearing this sound, the pirates immediately believed all the boys were dead in the cabin. They were terrified.

42
00:03:53.504 --> 00:04:00.709
Seeing the wild look in his men's eyes, Hook grew afraid they might turn on him again.

43
00:04:00.710 --> 00:04:05.559
"Lads, listen to me," he said, thinking quickly.

44
00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:10.635
"It's the girl! Our bad luck comes from having a girl on board.

45
00:04:10.636 --> 00:04:13.948
Everything will be right again when she's gone."

46
00:04:13.949 --> 00:04:17.139
The men thought for a moment.

47
00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:19.951
"He's right," Cookson said.

48
00:04:19.952 --> 00:04:24.424
"I recall an old saying about girls bringing bad luck."

49
00:04:24.425 --> 00:04:30.881
"Throw the girl overboard!" the pirates cried as they rushed to the mast.

50
00:04:30.882 --> 00:04:35.932
"No one can save you now, missy," Hook hissed to the figure in the cloak.

51
00:04:35.933 --> 00:04:40.395
"There's one that can save me," the figure replied.

52
00:04:40.396 --> 00:04:44.215
"Who's that?" Hook said.

53
00:04:44.216 --> 00:04:48.279
"Peter Pan, the avenger!" came the answer.

54
00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:55.906
And with those words, Peter flung off the cloak.
